SimonSays TODO

Before 0.7:
* BLOCKER - Finish field-testing the Gaze / Dwell-click automatic mode before release. Its evaluation timer was dead until 2026-09-21 (TIMER_DWELL_DETECT shared id 2 with FAST_TIMER_CHECK_ZORDER), so EvaluateDwellAutoMode() had no reachable caller and no Auto decision had ever been applied. Verified since: direct gaze on the 4C and Eye Tracker 5 (AC-17, AC-23, AC-36), tracking off -> Off (AC-20, AC-24), Tobii background services alone -> Off, a cursor tool -> MouseDwell and a clicking tool -> ExternalClick (AC-35, AC-37, 2026-10-23, the last two with stand-in processes). A machine with no tracker or tool -> Off (AC-3, 2026-10-26, another computer). Still unverified: AC-13 / REQ-F28 with a real cursor tool - Irisbond Hiru in mouse mode or OptiKey, no direct gaze - should resolve to MouseDwell within ~9 s (3-tick hysteresis). Update AC-13 and the Auto rows in the docs/specs/dwell.spec.md status matrix once done, and watch for Auto oscillation (REQ-N05).
* Gaze / Dwell-click: while the dwell window (`F3`) is open its forced mode applies to the whole app, so phrases in other windows can fire by dwell even with dwell saved as Off (REQ-F64). A probe-only override was tried on 2026-10-24 and reverted the same day because gaze dwell stopped working; find out why before retrying (one suspect: it was tested with the saved mode Off, where phrases not dwelling was the intended result). 2026-10-26 diagnosis: the saved mode was indeed Off (`Dwell Mode Selection` = 1 just before that test and right after the revert), and the "works, but after a few seconds" seen after the revert matches the window's 2 s refresh switching the whole app to gaze — so the override most likely worked as designed. To redo it, re-apply the same change and test with the saved mode both Auto (phrases dwell by gaze with the window open and closed) and Off (phrases never dwell; the LOOK probe still does). Simpler alternative: disable the other SimonSays windows while the dwell window is open.
* Gaze / Dwell-click: check the lock-on delay by gaze on a real board (AC-43 gaze part): scanning across phrases shows no progress-bar flicker and holding the gaze still activates. The timing itself was verified with the cursor (AC-41).

Before 1.0:
* Integrate eye-tracking (Windows Eye Control at minimum) to drive phrase selection and playback.
* Translate the restructured English HELP.md into the 16 docs/help/HELP_*.md files, then re-run scripts/build_help_html.ps1. This includes the new table of contents and section order (everyday use first, editing afterwards), the new sections (Default phrases, Using SimonSays in online meetings, Sounds included with SimonSays, Undoing changes, Where SimonSays keeps your files, Feedback, support and privacy), and the two older untranslated parts: "Customizing the look (board & category styles)" and the PNG/JPG icon-format note.
* Translate the updated icon-format Help note (PNG/JPG icons, HELP.md "Setting or changing a category icon") into the docs/help/HELP_*.md files, then re-run scripts/build_help_html.ps1.
* Translate the 0.7 Gaze / Dwell-click Help changes (English HELP.md only so far) into the docs/help/HELP_*.md files, then re-run scripts/build_help_html.ps1: the Eye Tracker 5 now listed as verified, the `Automatic` note about Tobii background software, `HID eye tracker` using gaze only, the `Lock-on delay` setting and the 500 ms default dwell time, the `Save diagnostic report...` button, and the "Tobii Eye Tracker 4C software" note on reinstalling Tobii Core 2.13.1.7294 (sections "Gaze / Dwell-click" and "Reporting eye-tracking hardware issues").
* Gaze / Dwell-click: resolve the Tobii Stream Engine field-of-use value passed on engine 4+ (`kFieldOfUseInteractive` = 1 in src/SSStreamEngine.cpp) from Tobii's own documentation; it is still unverified. Do not resolve it by probing the DLL (Tobii EULA v3.0 section 1.4).
* Categories window right-click menu: add entries that act on the clicked button itself (Edit `F4`, Add after `F7`, Delete `F8` for that category or phrase). CAT-F59 leaves the selection alone today (docs/specs/categories-phrases.spec.md section 18).
* Translate the 0.7 right-click menu Help changes (English HELP.md only so far) into the docs/help/HELP_*.md files, then re-run scripts/build_help_html.ps1: the new "Right-click menu" lines in "Categories window", the renamed `Show quick access buttons and menu` setting, and `Exit` asking first in "Tray icon menu".
* Add tooltips to the main window's quick access buttons (open a board, Settings). SSButton has no tooltip support at all, so this means a new BTN- feature (a TOOLTIPS_CLASS control owned by SSButton) plus two localized strings; today the buttons only carry a window text as their screen-reader name (settings.spec.md SET-N04).
* Have native speakers review the Gaze / Dwell-click terminology added in Arabic, Basque, Chinese, Hebrew, Hindi, Japanese, Korean and Russian (DWELL_* plus the board-style/delete-all confirmations and the IMPORT_LANGUAGE_* import warnings in include/localized_strings.h; the import warnings use a "File language: <name>" phrasing in these languages because the inserted native name cannot be inflected). The wording follows the conventions already used in the Romance-language tables, but terms like "HID eye tracker", "dwell-click" and "gaze-driven cursor" vary by locale, and this is the setup screen for users who can only operate the app by gaze. Check the Arabic and Hebrew dialog visually too (RTL layout with embedded Latin terms such as HID and Windows). Include the strings added in October 2026: the `Save diagnostic report...` button and its three status messages (DWELL_DUMP_BUTTON_ID, DWELL_STATUS_DUMP_*), the `Lock-on delay` label (DWELL_LOCKON_LABEL_ID), and the Tobii licence (medical use) note in each docs/help/HELP_*.md.
* Have native speakers check the two Conversation phrases added in 0.7 in all 18 languages: the short reaction of surprise or dismay (`Oh dear`, `Vaja!`, `Ene!`, `Oje!`, `عجباً!`, `אוי!`, `अरे!`, `哎呀！`, `おや！`, `이런!`...) and the `Never mind` phrase. Check the labels of the seven sounds added to `Sounds` in the same pass, above all the `Uh-uh` and `Rimshot` ones (few languages write them) and `Ahem` in Arabic and Hindi, where a descriptive noun was used instead. Interjections rarely translate literally.
* Have native speakers review the European Portuguese interface strings (PORTUGUESE_LOCALIZED_UI_STRINGS in include/localized_strings.h), the Brazilian Portuguese help (docs/help/HELP_pt_BR.md), and both Portuguese default phrase sets (include/default_phrases.h).

* Have native speakers review the ready-made categories in Arabic, Chinese, Hebrew, Hindi, Japanese, Korean and Russian (scripts/extra_boards/yes_no.json, pain_body.json, spelling.json, games.json, questions.json, daily_care.json, hearing_check.json, and the Fitzgerald Key translations in fitzgerald_key.json for Basque and Russian; have a clinician glance at the Daily care wording - suction, cough assist, tube feeding), then re-run scripts/build_extra_boards.ps1. Check also whether isolated letters (Korean jamo, Hindi consonants, Japanese kana) are read sensibly by each language's voice, and the Basque and Galician pain phrases.

Possible Long Term Goals:
* SSButton: gaze long-press (dwell) to click, with other color slower visual dwell progress indicator.
* Gaze / Dwell-click: support a 64-bit SimonSays build on machines whose Tobii software only installs a 32-bit engine (4C, PCEye 5), with a 32-bit counterpart of the SimonSaysGaze64 helper. Today the x64 build cannot read those trackers; the shipped 32-bit build reads both kinds.
* Accesible settings dialog for gaze users.
* Declare per-monitor DPI awareness. The app declares none, so Windows bitmap-scales it (blurry at 125%+); every layout is in 96-dpi logical pixels and would need scaling.
* Register the SimonSays bar as its own app bar (SHAppBarMessage ABM_NEW) so Windows reserves its space and maximized windows no longer extend under it; and place it clear of the Windows 11 Widgets button (docs/specs/taskbar.spec.md section 18).
* Sound effects library expansion and user customization options.
* Maybe: also set SimonSays' Windows per-app output device (the Volume mixer setting) to the `Sound output` choice, on top of the current routing (docs/specs/sound.spec.md SND-F70), so the PlaySound/MCI fallbacks follow it too and the setting is repaired at startup if Windows resets it. It uses the undocumented Windows.Media.Internal.AudioPolicyConfig factory (IAudioPolicyConfigFactory, Windows 10 21H2+ IID ab3d4648-e242-459f-b02f-541c70306324, SetPersistedDefaultAudioEndpoint for eConsole + eMultimedia); guard it at runtime (RoGetActivationFactory with that exact IID, then write + read back) and keep the current routing alone if either step fails. Tested 2026-10-14: WinMM only honours it in a process started AFTER the setting, so it takes effect from the next launch; while it is set, "Windows default" must open the real system default device explicitly instead of WAVE_MAPPER, or the running app stays on the old device. Clear it when "Windows default" is chosen (uninstalling does not).
* Flow fill: option to use the spare room in the category window to fill it with the following categories' phrases (a continuous, gap-free grid) instead of leaving empty space below the selected category's phrases.
